<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ladislaus of Naples</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1377–1414</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ladislaus of the Anjou-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/durres">Durazzo</a> house was King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naples">Naples</a> from 1386 until his death in 1414. He also claimed the crown of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sigismund-holy-roman-emperor">Sigismund of Luxembourg</a> and was crowned at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zadar">Zadar</a> in 1403, rewarding supporters such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hrvoje-vukcic-hrvatinic">Hrvoje Vukčić Hrvatinić</a>. Abandoning the struggle, he sold his rights over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dalmatia">Dalmatia</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> in 1409 for 100,000 ducats.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ladislaus-of-naples.jpg" alt="Ladislaus of Naples" width="250" height="331" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Cristofano dell'Altissimo · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ladislas_of_Naples_(head).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
